    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nConsolidated the three separate duplicate checks into one derived `identityKey`.\n\n**`identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`** \u2014 rejection with 409 now happens only when a new owner's *whole* key matches an existing owner's.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **`util/IdentityKeys.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive helper: `of(Owner)` derives the key (telephone is already stored E.164-normalized; missing email/householdId become empty segments) and `isDuplicate(...)` compares whole keys.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 replaced the three `if` blocks (telephone `anyMatch`, `EmailDuplicates.isDuplicate`, `!sharesHousehold && Households.isDuplicate`) with a single `IdentityKeys.isDuplicate` check, moving the existing `setHouseholdId` call above it so the household segment is part of the candidate's key.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` expression populates `identityKey` on every owner response via `IdentityKeys.of(owner)` (single source of truth, no per-endpoint wiring).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO exposes it.\n\n### Behaviour change confirmed\nBecause the telephone is in the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\n### Structural-impact notes\nThe behaviour lives in a new small class with near-zero surrounding complexity, so the only edit inside the large controller is a net **reduction** \u2014 three branches collapsed to one \u2014 rather than growth. The mapper edit is a single annotation on a CC-1 method. No existing method or class grew in complexity.",
